cff-version: 1.2.0

type: software

title: "CasTuner (Python Port): Reproducible modelling of repression and derepression dynamics"

version: "0.1.1"

date-released: "2025-10-29"

message: >
  If you use this repository, please cite both this software and the original
  CasTuner article listed in the references section.

  Software citation
  Mishra, A. (2025). CasTuner (Python Port): Reproducible modelling of repression/derepression dynamics (v0.1.1).
  GitHub. https://github.com/bibymaths/CasTuner — MIT License.

  Original CasTuner article
  Noviello, G., Gjaltema, R. A. F., & Schulz, E. G.
  CasTuner: a degron and CRISPR/Cas-based toolkit for analog tuning of endogenous gene expression.

abstract: >
  Independent Python reimplementation of the CasTuner analysis pipeline for
  CRISPR/Cas-based analog gene regulation. The workflow covers flow-cytometry
  preprocessing, kinetic parameter estimation (half-times, Hill curves),
  ODE-based repression and derepression simulations, uncertainty quantification,
  and global sensitivity analysis. The implementation preserves the logic of
  the original R workflow while adding Snakemake-based orchestration for
  end-to-end reproducibility and scalability.

